  "title": "packet-wow: Correct protocol_version field",
  "description": "Fixes a very small part of #11398.\n\nThe fields were incorrectly identified as error fields because Mangos,\nthe most popular open source emulator in 2009 incorrectly identified it\nas such.\n\nReverse engineering of the client revealed that the fields were protocol\nversions.\n\nAs well as misidentifying the field, the WOW_SERVER_TO_CLIENT version\nalso read the wrong field. The actual error field is the one that comes\nafter the protocol version field.\n\nCorrect packets are in Ember\nWOW_CLIENT_TO_SERVER\nhttps://github.com/EmberEmu/Ember/blob/03c130d3d6276e7032fc9e13c9d287ea7c6ed536/src/login/grunt/client/LoginChallenge.h#L39\n\nWOW_SERVER_TO_CLIENT\nhttps://github.com/EmberEmu/Ember/blob/03c130d3d6276e7032fc9e13c9d287ea7c6ed536/src/login/grunt/server/LoginChallenge.h#L33\n\nAs well as the Wiki\nhttps://wowdev.wiki/Packets/Login/Vanilla#Challenge_packets\n\nI included a capture in the issue, linked here for completeness:\n[wow-auth-realmlist.pcapng](/uploads/de2fa5d39ba1cbbc9c253004b782ffa1/wow-auth-realmlist.pcapng)\n\nAs I wrote in the issue I intend on implementing all the missing or misidentified fields for the 1.12 version of the protocol. The current implementation supports an unknown version of the protocol, and possibly not even a real version since it's missing fields that would have been in the 2.4.3 version it's probably based on, what is the policy on keeping backwards compatibility towards this unknown most likely non-existing version?\n\nImplementing the 1.12 version as the default would provide a better starting point for newer versions than the current implementation and would preemptively remove a bunch of legacy cruft that only really exists because information regarding the protocol was limited in 2009.",
  "state": "merged",
